{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"913cdb06348a3b71b7009dac7b313a3661b4aac3ec9a934b3164944a442b44d8","digest":{"component_or_area":"unit test: wiki_render_hardening","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer","_EQUIVALENCE_CHUNK","test_the_equivalence_chunks_cover_every_renderable_unit","--timeout=300","--timeout-method=thread",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","_renderable_units","_convert","_legacy_convert"],"problem_keywords":["test timeout","pytest-xdist worker crash","macOS CI flakiness","unbounded test cost","pandoc spawning"],"propositions":["A single test function walks 884 corpus units with ~1768 serial pandoc spawns, taking 91.6s idle and 504.8s under CPU saturation, crossing CI's 300s per-test timeout on the macOS runner.","pytest-timeout's thread method calls os._exit(1) when the budget is exhausted, killing the xdist worker outright with no traceback rather than failing the test.","The test's monolithic loop structure binds its cost to corpus size, so growth cannot be prevented by chunking after the fact.","Chunk-parametrization with fixed batch size _EQUIVALENCE_CHUNK=40 bounds each test case independently and allows xdist to parallelize across workers.","All 884 units remain compared byte-identically against the oracle with real pandoc; the fix closes only the per-test cost, not the equivalence property."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787294319902848001,"uuid":"0699adb2-a666-406e-985d-3d8802419648"}